ITAR='https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-22/chapter-I/subchapter-M/part-120/subpart-C/section-120.50'
pages={
'zh':[
('offer-review','Offer 写了出口许可条件','弄清雇主是否已经提交 EL 申请，以及等待结果会怎样影响入职日期。',[
('先确认进度','招聘人员说“在等 EL”时，可以问公司目前是在确认是否需要申请，还是已经向主管部门提交申请。请对方区分岗位评估、材料准备和等待决定三个阶段。'),
('弄清许可涉及什么','请招聘人员把问题转给公司的出口合规团队。可以提供公开的岗位说明，由公司确认涉及的技术、适用法规及是否有可用授权。个人不必根据“芯片工程师”这个职位名称自行推断。'),
('把下一步落实到日期','向招聘方确认 offer 的截止日、下一次进度更新的日期，以及如果许可届时仍在审理，公司是否能调整入职时间。开工日期以雇主书面确认为准。')],[(BIS,'美国商务部 BIS · 视同出口申请指南')]),
('residency','加拿大 PR 与美国绿卡','看懂两种永久居民身份怎样影响美国岗位的视同出口判断。',[
('在美国接触受控技术','EAR §734.13(a)(2) 涵盖在美国向外国人披露受管制技术或源代码。§734.13(b) 用最近取得的国籍或永久居民身份所属国家确定视同出口目的地。'),
('中国籍，后来取得加拿大 PR','如果加拿大 PR 是最近取得且仍维持的身份，EAR 对这次披露通常按加拿大判断。雇主仍要根据技术分类及适用限制确认是否需要许可。加拿大工签或学签本身不能代替永久居民身份。'),
('美国绿卡的作用','美国合法永久居民通常属于出口管制所称的 U.S. person。向其本人在美国披露技术，一般无需外国人员视同出口许可。军品技术资料适用 ITAR 时有另一套国别规则。')],[(EAR,'15 CFR §734.13 · EAR 国别规则'),(CHART,'15 CFR Part 738 · 分类与国家表'),(DOJ,'美国司法部 · 招聘与出口管制'),(ITAR,'22 CFR §120.50 · ITAR 国别规则')]),
('recruiter-questions','和招聘方怎么沟通','给 recruiter 和合规团队的三个问题，附可直接使用的英文问法。',[
('先问岗位','“Which responsibilities or technologies in this role may require an export license?” 请对方说明需要评估的是哪部分工作职责。只讨论公开的岗位范围。'),
('再问身份材料','“Which citizenship or permanent residence details does your export compliance team need, and through which secure channel?” 如果持有加拿大 PR，请一并说明取得顺序与目前状态。'),
('最后问进度','“Has the company submitted an export license application for this role yet? When should we check in again about my start date?” 留存对方的回复和下一次跟进日期。')],[(BIS,'BIS · 申请材料与技术说明'),(DOJ,'美国司法部 · 出口合规评估与工作资格核验')])],
'en':[
('offer-review','An offer subject to export clearance','Understand an internal review, a license application and what each means for your start date.',[
('Find out where the review stands','When a recruiter says an offer is waiting on an export license, ask whether the company is assessing the role, preparing an application or waiting for a government decision. Each stage has a different next step.'),
('Identify the access involved','Share the public job description with recruiting. Ask the employer’s export compliance team to confirm the relevant technology, applicable rules and any authorization that covers the proposed access. A chip design job title alone cannot settle the question.'),
('Agree on a follow-up date','Ask when the offer expires, when the team will update you and whether the start date can move if the review continues. Use the employer’s written confirmation when planning your start date.')],[(BIS,'BIS guidance on deemed export applications')]),
('residency','Canadian PR and a U.S. green card','How permanent residence can affect a deemed export assessment for a U.S. semiconductor role.',[
('The U.S. workplace rule','EAR §734.13(a)(2) covers releasing controlled technology or source code to a foreign person in the United States. Under §734.13(b), the destination follows the most recent country of citizenship or permanent residency.'),
('Chinese citizenship followed by Canadian PR','If Canadian permanent residency is the most recent qualifying status and remains valid, Canada generally supplies the destination for this EAR analysis. The employer still checks the technology classification and other applicable restrictions. Temporary Canadian work or study permits do not confer PR.'),
('U.S. permanent residence','A lawful permanent resident of the United States generally qualifies as a U.S. person for these rules. Releasing technology to that person in the United States generally does not require a foreign-person deemed export license. ITAR has separate nationality rules for defense technical data.')],[(EAR,'15 CFR §734.13 · EAR export definition'),(CHART,'15 CFR Part 738 · Classification and country chart'),(DOJ,'U.S. Department of Justice · Export controls and hiring'),(ITAR,'22 CFR §120.50 · ITAR export definition')]),
('recruiter-questions','Questions for your recruiter','Three questions to take to recruiting and the employer’s export compliance team.',[
('Ask about responsibilities','“Which responsibilities or technologies in this role may require an export license?” Keep the conversation at the level of the public job description.'),
('Ask about documentation','“Which citizenship or permanent residence details does your export compliance team need, and through which secure channel?” If you hold Canadian PR, include the order in which you acquired your statuses and whether they remain current.'),
('Ask about timing','“Has the company submitted an export license application for this role yet? When should we check in again about my start date?” Keep a copy of the answer and the agreed follow-up date.')],[(BIS,'BIS · Deemed export application requirements'),(DOJ,'U.S. Department of Justice · Export compliance assessments')])]}
